menu "Desk proxy"

    config LOCTEK_PROXY_DRY_RUN
        bool "Decode and account for movement commands without sending them"
        default n
        help
            Commands are decoded, the deadman runs and status goes back to the
            panel, but the frames that would actually move the desk are held
            back and logged instead. For testing the whole path with the desk
            standing still.

    config PROXY_LED_BT_GPIO
        int "BT indicator LED GPIO ('BT' on the silkscreen), -1 if unwired"
        default 32
        help
            Drives one of the two LEDs inside the RJ45 jack through a 220R
            series resistor. GPIO32 on the carrier board (row B pin 6, D32).
            Solid while a panel is connected, heartbeat while advertising.

            GPIO32/33 double as the external 32 kHz crystal pins. They are free
            as GPIO only while the RTC runs off the internal RC, which is the
            default and what this build uses.

    config PROXY_LED_DESK_GPIO
        int "Desk indicator LED GPIO ('LINK' on the silkscreen), -1 if unwired"
        default 33
        help
            The other jack LED. GPIO33 on the carrier board (row B pin 7, D33).
            Solid while the control box answers; fast blink when bytes arrive
            but no frame decodes, which is a baud or wiring fault rather than
            silence.

    config PROXY_LED_SELFTEST
        bool "Blink both LEDs at boot"
        default y
        help
            Each LED on its own, then both together. Lets a loose LED clipped to
            one pin prove that pin before the board exists.

endmenu
